And it's really they're going to know the difference between how they're treated, you know, really not by me or Parnoff, but by me and my team or their team. Most people leave the dental practice because of the team, not because of the doctor, you know, because it's usually the team that they're responding with.

01:39:41.000 --> 01:39:58.000
So I have never taken insurance. So I started in 1985, and I was the sixth periodontist in the town of 65,000 people. So I opened up my hometown, which was saturated, and I decided I was going to develop a.

